  "notes": "Fixed brain budget decay no-op bug in runDecay() (debt-manager.ts). Root cause: shouldRun guard used total linesBefore (exempt+decayable) instead of decayable-only audit. Steps 4 and 5 also used countBrainLines() (total) for their inner guards, so when DECISIONS.md (702 lines, exempt) dominated the total, trim was either wrongly triggered or stuck in a loop. Fix: (1) shouldRun now uses audit.status === 'OVER' (decayableLines > budget) only, dropping the incorrect linesBefore > budget fallback; (2) step 4 re-audits mid-decay (auditMid) and guards on auditMid.decayableLines > budget; (3) step 5 re-audits (auditFinal) and guards on auditFinal.decayableLines > budget. This ensures exempt files (DECISIONS.md, PROJECT-IDENTITY.md) are never counted against the decay threshold. Created tests/orchestra/memory-decay.test.ts with 10 tests covering: auditBrainBudget correctness (5 tests) + runDecay exempt-aware budget logic (5 tests) including the key regression scenario (exempt 702 + eligible 500, budget 300 → decay triggers). All 32 decay-related tests pass (brain-budget-decay + memory-decay + learning-decay). The 115 pre-existing failures in brain.test.ts etc. are Task 137-001 scope — not introduced by this fix.",
